#: processes/sdlc/test-data-curation.bpmn:138
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Parse the file with `discriminateTestDataSet` (`schemas/test-data.ts`) to confirm a consumer can tell fixed from generated from the file content alone (never the path), verify `verifyGeneratedSetDigest` on generated sets, and bind the resulting `TestDataRef` (`toTestDataRef`) into the `test-plan/v1` case."
msgstr ""

#: processes/sdlc/test-data-curation.bpmn:168
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Process_BeanClose: end the bean in a state that says why — complete and archive it, scrap it with its reasons and archive it, or record the blocker and hand it back. The one place resolve and archive are drawn; placed straight before the end so the engine's resolve sees nothing left but the archive step."
msgstr ""

#: processes/sdlc/test-data-curation.bpmn:152
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Process_BeanOpen: check before you create, find out whose the bean is, and claim it — or leave it alone when it is someone else's. The one place a claim is drawn; the gateway after this reads which end it reached."
msgstr ""

#: processes/sdlc/test-data-curation.bpmn:158
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Reads which end Process_BeanOpen reached. `claimed`: the bean is in progress and this process works it. `not yours`: a sibling session or a human holds it, nothing was written to it, and this process stops here rather than work a bean it does not own (bean-coordination)."
msgstr ""

#: processes/sdlc/test-data-curation.bpmn:122
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Record `contentType`, `specialisation`, `template`, `params`, `seed`, and the canonical `sha256` digest (`computeGeneratedSetDigest`) with `$schema: \"test-data-generated/1.0.0\"` and `kind: \"generated\"` in the instance's declared `test-data-generated` directory. Never store materialised records."
msgstr ""

